# Interactive Video Marker Implementation

You are right—typing numbers into a box is a friction point. We will upgrade the "Selective Preview" section to be a high-interaction "Mark-Capture" system.

## Proposed Changes

### [MODIFY] [main_ui.py](file:///c:/just-dub-it2/app/main_ui.py)
**Objective**: Build the JavaScript Marker Bridge.

1. **Hardware ID Branding**: Assign a unique `elem_id` to the main video acquisition component.
2. **The "Mark" Logic (JavaScript)**:
   - Create a JS shim that listens to the browser's HTML5 video player.
   - It will surgically extract the `currentTime` of your playback.
3. **The "Mark" Buttons**:
   - Replace the manual number boxes with an interactive row:
     - **Button: 📍 Set Start**: Instantly grabs the video's current second and sets it as the Start Point.
     - **Button: 🏁 Set Stop**: Grabs the current second and automatically calculates the **Duration** relative to your start point.
4. **Iterative Flow**: 
   - You play the video -> Hit **📍 Set Start** at the beginning of the scene -> Play until the end -> Hit **🏁 Set Stop** -> Hit **🎬 Preview Selective Scene**.

## User Review Required
> [!NOTE]
> This uses a **JavaScript Capture Bridge**. Because Gradio runs Python on your server and Video in your browser, the "capture" happens the millisecond you click the button. 
> 
> Does this "Two-Button Marking" system (Start/Stop) align with how you want to interact with the project?
